--- stdout
Compile a Spago workspace from an entry point to a single Go program.

Usage: googoo go [FLAGS] [DIR] [-- ARGUMENTS]…

Arguments:
  [DIR]            Directory to write main.go to. Without one, builds the executable that `googoo run` runs and prints
                   its path.
  [-- ARGUMENTS]…  Arguments for the --profile run. Defaults to run.execArgs.

Flags:
  -p, --package <NAME>           Workspace package to compile.
      --entry <MODULE.NAME>      Qualified entry point. Defaults to Main.main, or without DIR to the one `googoo run`
                                 uses.
      --no-line-directives       Leaves out of the Go written to DIR the //line comments that make stack traces,
                                 debuggers and profiles point at your .purs files.
      --line-directives <WHICH>  Which Go lines name their .purs line: `every` puts a //line comment in front of each
                                 statement and declaration, for tools that show each Go line next to its PureScript.
                                 [possible values: sparse, every]
      --pgo <PROFILE>            Optimise the executable for this CPU profile (go build -pgo), or `off` to leave out the
                                 one --profile recorded.
      --profile                  Run the program once while recording a CPU profile, keep it in .spago/go/<package>/
                                 default.pgo and build again optimised for it. Later builds use it until --pgo off.
  -h, --help                     Print help
--- stderr
